{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1039144-new-to-geist-lots-of-questions","id":1039144,"title":"New to Geist - Lots of Questions","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Geist: The Sin-Eaters"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-01-27T15:51:23-08:00","id":1039144,"title":"New to Geist - Lots of Questions","content":"Hello, I am new to Geist and I have alot of questions.<br /> <br /> #1) If they come back from the dead are they truly alive? - <span style=\"color:blue\">This was answered but to be complete I added it here.</span><br /> #2) If truly alive do they function as any other living being (Heartbeat, Eat, Bodily functions, ETC...)?<br /> #3) Will their blood sustain a Vampire?<br /> #4) Do the have their soul and if so does it have marks of death upon it?<br /> #5) If they have a hitchhiker in a Geist that they have made a deal with can that Geist be separated/pulled way from the living person, and they remain living?<br /> #6) Can they father a child/get pregnant and if so is their progeny affected by the Geist that inhabits them?<br /> #7) If living can they be turned into a Vampire or become awakened?<br /> <br /> This is just the beginning and I will have more based upon the answer and how much I learn about the system.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-27T16:32:05-08:00","id":1039150,"title":"","content":"Can't speak for anything that might potentially change in the upcoming second edition, of course. From a first edition standpoint:<br /> <br /> 1) They're alive, but carry the aspect of death, meaning effects that differentiate between living and undead are kind of finicky about the Bound. For instance, the Old Laws of the Kerberoi treat them as living, I believe, while the possessing powers of the vampiric strix don't require their full ability to possess the living in order to inhabit the Bound.<br /> 2) They're biologically alive, although their blood also carries ectoplasmic traces that act like an auxiliary immune system, and they are able to maintain consciousness regardless of any injury short of death. They eat, they sleep, their heart beats.<br /> 3) Sure. Those ectoplasmic traces might cause some form of side effect, but I don't believe any book has addressed it, so it's Storyteller fiat.<br /> 4) Not sure what you mean by death marks. They have a soul, but it may or may not necessarily still resemble a human soul.<br /> 5) Yes, but they lose access to a number of aspects of the Sin-Eater template, and it generally seems to be a traumatic experience. See page 243.<br /> 6) Yes, Sin-Eaters are fertile. Nothing has been written on the subject of their children being anything but normal humans.<br /> 7) No. Generally, any process that imbues a major character template depends upon the stable, normal condition of the human soul. Glue a geist onto the thing and the blood of the Embrace doesn't know what the hell.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-27T17:15:38-08:00","id":1039170,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stupid Loserman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1039144-new-to-geist-lots-of-questions?p=1039150#post1039150\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2) They're biologically alive, although their blood also carries ectoplasmic traces that act like an auxiliary immune system, and they are able to maintain consciousness regardless of any injury short of death. They eat, they sleep, their heart beats.</div> </div> </div> </div>And while death will make them go unconcious, if the Geist wants to keep the deal going, they'll just wake up the next day anyway. Only slightly worse for wear.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-27T17:30:13-08:00","id":1039173,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stupid Loserman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1039144-new-to-geist-lots-of-questions?p=1039150#post1039150\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">4) Not sure what you mean by death marks. They have a soul, but it may or may not necessarily still resemble a human soul.</div> </div> </div> </div>The CoD system that I know best is Mage, The Death Mage can look at the souls of the living and look to see if they have any number of marks, listed below. Would the Sin-Eater register as having their soul messed with.<br /> <br /> The Geist inside them would fall under the purview of a Death Mage, can the Death Mage attack the Geist without harming the host or are they more or less one entity. I am interested in how they would interact with the other CoD supernaturals.<br /> <br /> And just what they are physically, example: They are inhabited by a Geist, does that allow then to reach across into the Twilight and attach full ghosts. I am assuming that since they are truly living that they are in the physical world and not in the Twilight world.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mage: the Awakening page 128, Soul Marks (Death \u2022)</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">She can discern<br /> the presence of Persistent Conditions, if the subject is Awakened, if<br /> the subject is a supernatural being, if the subject has created a soul<br /> stone (see \u201cSoul Stones\u201d p. 98), if the subject has had her soul tampered<br /> with, if the subject is Possessed, the presence of any Gnosis 5+<br /> Legacy Attainments, if the subject has eaten or otherwise consumed<br /> another\u2019s soul, or if the subject is suffering from a Paradox Condition.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12802,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","user":"Hardwire99","date":". 01-27-2017, 08:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-27T22:28:26-08:00","id":1039264,"title":"","content":"Geist 1E doesn't mention anything specific about soul &quot;markings&quot; or how they may register to other supernaturals. Ghosts always recognize Sin-Eaters for what they are, although how/why is left somewhat vague. At this point, I'd say most of those are up to the ST. If you're going strictly by what's mentioned in the books, the mage should recognize that Sin-Eaters are supernatural and possessed. I only say the possessed part because some sections in <i>Hunter: Mortal Remains</i> discussing the Lucifuge and Malleus Maleficarum determine that Sin-Eaters are, in fact, possessed but immune to exorcism.<br /> <br /> Page 230 of the Geist rulebook details the conflict between &quot;Sin-Eater versus Self (or Geist).&quot; Bound are called Bound because they are bound to their geists at the level of the soul, and attacking a Sin-Eater's geist would absolutely hurt both, just as forcibly removing a geist from its Bound is damaging to the Sin-Eater.<br /> <br /> I wouldn't go so far as to say they're one entity, because geists are capable of willingly releasing a Bound from their contract without the Sin-Eater dying; it's mentioned in a tiny section without any examples, explanation, or resulting aftermath given (hopefully something that will be rectified with 2E). The 1E rulebook discusses it a little in some different areas, but the overall picture I got was that it really is like a possession by an ephemeral entity, just a little bit deeper and involving soul-fusion. If ghost possession is like sticking on a bandaid, geist contracts are like surgically embedding the bandaid into your skin. Depending on the level of synergy, the drives and agendas of either side will affect the other, and depending on the strength of their wills and how compatible they are, it could be either a constant battle for control or a partnership.<br /> <br /> See page 175: &quot;In a sort of reverse possession, the Sin-Eater seizes the full senses of his geist, pouring his consciousness into the alien creature bound to him. This allows a Sin-Eater to see into and physically interact with Twilight at the cost of losing some sense of his physical surroundings. Of course, by opening himself up to Twilight, a Sin-Eater places himself in a position where ghosts can interact with him as well...In this state, a Sin-Eater can combat a ghost that hasn\u2019t manifested and can manipulate Twilight objects. Only the body of a Sin-Eater makes the translation. Any physical weapons held by the Sin-Eater at the time are left behind, along with his flesh and bone...Combating an unmanifested ghost is apt to draw some strange looks from bystanders. Instead of a life-or-death contest, normal humans only see some weirdo slashing and flailing around him at imaginary foes. Fortunately, attacks made in Twilight remain in Twilight, unless someone walks directly into the Sin-Eater and takes an elbow or fist to the face.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/2.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12708-chesh","name":"Chesh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12708_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"238"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-28T03:53:50-08:00","id":1039346,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chesh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1039144-new-to-geist-lots-of-questions?p=1039264#post1039264\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Geist 1E doesn't mention anything specific about soul &quot;markings&quot; or how they may register to other supernaturals. Ghosts always recognize Sin-Eaters for what they are, although how/why is left somewhat vague. At this point, I'd say most of those are up to the ST. If you're going strictly by what's mentioned in the books, the mage should recognize that Sin-Eaters are supernatural and possessed. I only say the possessed part because some sections in <i>Hunter: Mortal Remains</i> discussing the Lucifuge and Malleus Maleficarum determine that Sin-Eaters are, in fact, possessed but immune to exorcism.<br /> <br /> Page 230 of the Geist rulebook details the conflict between &quot;Sin-Eater versus Self (or Geist).&quot; Bound are called Bound because they are bound to their geists at the level of the soul, and attacking a Sin-Eater's geist would absolutely hurt both, just as forcibly removing a geist from its Bound is damaging to the Sin-Eater.<br /> <br /> I wouldn't go so far as to say they're one entity, because geists are capable of willingly releasing a Bound from their contract without the Sin-Eater dying; it's mentioned in a tiny section without any examples, explanation, or resulting aftermath given (hopefully something that will be rectified with 2E). The 1E rulebook discusses it a little in some different areas, but the overall picture I got was that it really is like a possession by an ephemeral entity, just a little bit deeper and involving soul-fusion. If ghost possession is like sticking on a bandaid, geist contracts are like surgically embedding the bandaid into your skin. Depending on the level of synergy, the drives and agendas of either side will affect the other, and depending on the strength of their wills and how compatible they are, it could be either a constant battle for control or a partnership.<br /> <br /> See page 175: &quot;In a sort of reverse possession, the Sin-Eater seizes the full senses of his geist, pouring his consciousness into the alien creature bound to him. This allows a Sin-Eater to see into and physically interact with Twilight at the cost of losing some sense of his physical surroundings. Of course, by opening himself up to Twilight, a Sin-Eater places himself in a position where ghosts can interact with him as well...In this state, a Sin-Eater can combat a ghost that hasn\u2019t manifested and can manipulate Twilight objects. Only the body of a Sin-Eater makes the translation. Any physical weapons held by the Sin-Eater at the time are left behind, along with his flesh and bone...Combating an unmanifested ghost is apt to draw some strange looks from bystanders. Instead of a life-or-death contest, normal humans only see some weirdo slashing and flailing around him at imaginary foes. Fortunately, attacks made in Twilight remain in Twilight, unless someone walks directly into the Sin-Eater and takes an elbow or fist to the face.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Ok since you are quoting 1e I bought the book, I was going to wait until 2e came out but what the heck it is only money.<br /> <br /> So based on what you have said and reading the 1e a little I would have to say that the Death Mage would look at it as just another possession until he started to try and extract the Geist then he would find out that there was something special, but not really knowing what, about this possession. And, in 1e at least, he is not able to exorcise the Geist. I would also guess that there would be some kind of Clash of Will if a Mage/Vampire/Werewolf/ETC were to attempt to alter the soul of the Sin-Eater in any way. With Sever Soul (Death \u2022\u2022\u2022) you could remove that soul of a normal human but to affect the soul of an Mage it would take Sever the Awakened Soul (Death \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022), it has already been stated that it would take a similar spell to remove the soul of a Vampire so I would imagine that it would be that same for a Sin-Eater.<br /> <br /> I was also reading the Post &quot;What We Know So Far: Geist the Sin-Eater 2nd Edition&quot; and I see that the Sin-Eater consumes plasm (the residue left behind by a ghost) in mage that description is called Ectoplasm, so I wonder if it is the same thing, I would assume since they are trying to make the systems compatible to allow for mixing the systems it would be the same but we will see.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert D</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1032849-what-we-know-so-far-geist-the-sin-eater-2nd-edition#post1032849\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> As the Bargain makes Sin-Eaters partially ghostly, they can physically eat ghosts, EVEN if it isn\u2019t manifesting. They convert the ghost\u2019s ephemera into Plasm as it\u2019s being eaten.</div> </div> </div> </div>Would lead me to believe that they will be able to physically attack a Ghost even while it is in Twilight.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert D</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1032849-what-we-know-so-far-geist-the-sin-eater-2nd-edition#post1032849\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Powers: 2<sup>nd</sup> edition powers are not called Manifestations (that\u2019s the 2<sup>nd</sup> Ed. Ephemeral entities abilities now), they are called Haunts. Keys are still a part of powers, but work differently than before (the old way made too many athematic powers and the grid system made adding new powers too difficult in 1<sup>st</sup> Edition).</div> </div> </div> </div>Then he goes on to say this<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert D</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1032849-what-we-know-so-far-geist-the-sin-eater-2nd-edition#post1032849\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Geists: Pretty direct beings. Not big on dissimulation. They are Rank 3+ ghosts. Most gain rank 3+ by drinking deep from one of the rivers of the Underworld. Anchors the ghost to a CONCEPT of death instead of just their old life\u2019s anchors (harder to blast them back to Underworld once they escape, which they may do through a Bargain, by a Gate, or other means. Lost of Geist have no Bargain-host). Exceptions: A) 1<sup>st</sup> person interred in any cemetery rises as a geist to serve as its guardian. B) Some occult rituals might do the trick, C) sometimes it just happens with no clear cause. Geists CAN use the Claimed Manifestation on a living person or a dead body IF it knows that manifestation. Bargain is a separate manifestation. (ephemeral entities have Twilight Form and a number of additional Manifestations equal to Rank). Geist-claimed ARE NOT THE SAME as Bound. Topic for the future books: Multiple Geists Bargaining with a single Bound. Geist CANNOT possess you, as part of the Bargain. They are also DEFINITELY NOT 100% under the Bound\u2019s control.</div> </div> </div> </div>This part is a little confusing as the Geist is still a ghost itself and therefore an Ephemeral Entity I realize that the physical host is not but the Geist should still have Manifestation powers. In Mage they call out a Rank 3 Ghost as a Geist so that matches up. I can only conclude that when a Geist becomes BOUND to a willing recipient that through the Bargain the energies used to activate the manifestation are transformed into the powers called Haunts. Therefore while bonded to the other soul the Geist would lose the abilities of Manifestation. If the bond is broken then everything goes back to being the same. I would also surmise that the Bargain is not a possession but more of a cohabitation or a special melding.<br /> <br /> So addressing what I said above about the Mage looking at it as just another possession, I will revise that to say that the Mage would probably look at it as a soul that was tampered with and not a possession. It looks like the Bargain makes all the difference in this case, changing the Geist and the Host granting powers and abilities in the \u201cBargain\u201d.<br /> <br /> I think that I am getting a picture of 2e Geist and how they will play with the other supernaturals in the CofD system.<br /> <br /> I see that someone mentioned Numina and I wonder if the bargaining Geist also loses his Numina, as Numina/Manifestation are bargained away for these Haunt powers. I suppose that he Haunt powers could just be an enhanced version of the Numina/Manifestations that a Geist would normally have. The Geist \u201cMelding\u201d with a living, willing, soul has supercharged those abilities, just speculation on my part as I think aloud. The only way to find out is to see when the books come out or if a Dev decides to drop in and comment.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-30T01:51:01-08:00","id":1040494,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hardwire99</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1039144-new-to-geist-lots-of-questions#post1039144\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hello, I am new to Geist and I have alot of questions.<br /> <br /> #1) If they come back from the dead are they truly alive? - <span style=\"color:blue\">This was answered but to be complete I added it here.</span><br /> #2) If truly alive do they function as any other living being (Heartbeat, Eat, Bodily functions, ETC...)?<br /> #3) Will their blood sustain a Vampire?<br /> #4) Do the have their soul and if so does it have marks of death upon it?<br /> #5) If they have a hitchhiker in a Geist that they have made a deal with can that Geist be separated/pulled way from the living person, and they remain living?<br /> #6) Can they father a child/get pregnant and if so is their progeny affected by the Geist that inhabits them?<br /> #7) If living can they be turned into a Vampire or become awakened?<br /> <br /> This is just the beginning and I will have more based upon the answer and how much I learn about the system.</div> </div> </div> </div>1) Yes<br /> 2) Yes<br /> 3) Yes<br /> 4) Yes<br /> 5) No<br /> 6) Yes to the first part, no to the second<br /> 7) No","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Travis Stout<br /> Geist 2e Developer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12259-gimpinblack","name":"GimpInBlack","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"81"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-30T02:44:33-08:00","id":1040509,"title":"","content":"They are still two separate entities correct? Do they have two separate thought patterns, minds, emotions, wants, desires, etc. If someone was able to detect an Ephemeral Entity would they be able to distinguish the Geist from the Person. As an example there are alot of supernatural beings that have the abilities to detect, see and interact with Ghosts and other Ephemeral Entities. Can they directly target the Geist or is the Geist immune to the powers of others while he is held up inside the host. Can the Bargain be ended by another, example a Death Mage has purview over the concept endings, end a spell, end an argument, even end a pact if the spell is strong enough? Can a Mind Mage target just the mind of the Geist and compel it to end the contract? Can a Necromancer Vampire use its abilities to control just the Geist?<br /> <br /> I ask these questions because I intend to start a game of Geist when 2e hits and i want to know how they mesh with the rest of the CofD. And i would also like to add them to the Current Mage game that I am running.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-30T03:06:50-08:00","id":1040520,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hardwire99</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1039144-new-to-geist-lots-of-questions?p=1040509#post1040509\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They are still two separate entities correct? Do they have two separate thought patterns, minds, emotions, wants, desires, etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd say yes, since that's the whole point of the Synergy trait. However, they're still fused on a soul-deep level, so I'd expect subtle bleedover. Like how people can have changed personalities after many years or a defining moment. You are still you, but different.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If someone was able to detect an Ephemeral Entity would they be able to distinguish the Geist from the Person. As an example there are alot of supernatural beings that have the abilities to detect, see and interact with Ghosts and other Ephemeral Entities. Can they directly target the Geist or is the Geist immune to the powers of others while he is held up inside the host. </div> </div> </div>I'd say immune to detection and interaction while inside the host, and the bundle would look like some weird fusion of ghost and human. This, however, will almost definitely be changed when we get the actual Geist 2E update content spoiled. Till then, your guess is as good as mine.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Can the Bargain be ended by another, example a Death Mage has purview over the concept endings, end a spell, end an argument, even end a pact if the spell is strong enough? Can a Mind Mage target just the mind of the Geist and compel it to end the contract? Can a Necromancer Vampire use its abilities to control just the Geist? </div> </div> </div>Nope. No way. Regular mages will never be able to de-template another supernatural being with their powers, or directly create one. The out-of-universe reason is for preventing situations where mages stomp through other people and their gamelines. The in-universe reason is that mages aren't quite all-knowing or all-mighty as they wish to be, and have defined limits to their magic that are often put in place by supernatural forces and entities that are too vast for them to act against, such as Mother Luna or the Principle or the Dark Mother.<br /> <br /> Unless you consider killing them as a way of ending the Bargain. Then Death Masters can just rip out the Geist and/or the mortal soul.<br /> <br /> Archmages can de-template others or slap templates on them, but they're explicitly breaking the rules intended for &quot;normal' levels of play. And even then, they still may face repercussions or unintended consequences.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I ask these questions because I intend to start a game of Geist when 2e hits and i want to know how they mesh with the rest of the CofD. And i would also like to add them to the Current Mage game that I am running. </div> </div> </div>They mesh as well as other supernaturals already do. From a Mage perspective, they're a not-easily solved Mystery for mages to Obsess over. A player might find it frustrating that they can't toy with other supernatural forces for what it seems to be arbitrarily put restrictions, until they figure out that an out-of-context Mystery that's not easily solved after a few moments of Mage Sight or throwing spells at it is an excellent source of character growth, in the form of Arcane Beats. In fact, that's the in-universe attitude of mages too - when they find a phenomenon that defies their model of reality, their eyes gleam with excitement. (Or fear, whichever comes first.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-30T03:17:08-08:00","id":1040523,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1039144-new-to-geist-lots-of-questions?p=1040520#post1040520\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They mesh as well as other supernaturals already do. From a Mage perspective, they're a not-easily solved Mystery for mages to Obsess over. A player might find it frustrating that they can't toy with other supernatural forces for what it seems to be arbitrarily put restrictions, until they figure out that an out-of-context Mystery that's not easily solved after a few moments of Mage Sight or throwing spells at it is an excellent source of character growth, in the form of Arcane Beats. In fact, that's the in-universe attitude of mages too - when they find a phenomenon that defies their model of reality, their eyes gleam with excitement. (Or fear, whichever comes first.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks for the answers, this I can work with and it will help to set the stage in the current game without the 2e Geist (still plan on buying it), set it as a mystery that they has to unravel and when the 2e book comes out then let them manipulate the mystery to get a closer look. So in my current game (actually haven't started it yet) I can count this mystery as ready.<br /> <br /> Really looking forward to the Geist 2e stuff.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-30T04:42:46-08:00","id":1040560,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1039144-new-to-geist-lots-of-questions?p=1040520#post1040520\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nope. No way. Regular mages will never be able to de-template another supernatural being with their powers, or directly create one. The out-of-universe reason is for preventing situations where mages stomp through other people and their gamelines. The in-universe reason is that mages aren't quite all-knowing or all-mighty as they wish to be, and have defined limits to their magic that are often put in place by supernatural forces and entities that are too vast for them to act against, such as Mother Luna or the Principle or the Dark Mother.<br /> <br /> Unless you consider killing them as a way of ending the Bargain. Then Death Masters can just rip out the Geist and/or the mortal soul.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fun fact, 2e mages can kind of de-template someone with time. If they use (I think) temporal summoning from a time before the creature gained its template, then the creature loses its template for the duration of the spell.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6365-fumus","name":"Fumus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6365_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-30T05:00:55-08:00","id":1040564,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fumus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1039144-new-to-geist-lots-of-questions?p=1040560#post1040560\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Fun fact, 2e mages can kind of de-template someone with time. If they use (I think) temporal summoning from a time before the creature gained its template, then the creature loses its template for the duration of the spell.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm pretty sure Temporal Summoning has two restrictions - it cannot bring the dead back to life, or undo supernatural transformation. It only changes the subject physically, so you can only do things like make an adult corpse into a child corpse, or make a vampire physically younger (which is itself quite a feat, but I digress)<br /> <br /> On the another hand, I just browsed through and found that another spell, Rewrite History, actually can undo even template transformation with its +2 Reach option. Make its Duration indefinite, and hope no one comes to dispel it or something.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-30T05:10:27-08:00","id":1040570,"title":"","content":"So then Mages do have the ability to de-template someone with an Unmaking spell. So I would also put an ending spell from death in that same category if it targets the Bargain.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-30T05:11:20-08:00","id":1040571,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1039144-new-to-geist-lots-of-questions?p=1040564#post1040564\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm pretty sure Temporal Summoning has two restrictions - it cannot bring the dead back to life, or undo supernatural transformation. It only changes the subject physically, so you can only do things like make an adult corpse into a child corpse, or make a vampire physically younger (which is itself quite a feat, but I digress)<br /> <br /> On the another hand, I just browsed through and found that another spell, Rewrite History, actually can undo even template transformation with its +2 Reach option. Make its Duration indefinite, and hope no one comes to dispel it or something.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I think temporal summoning is still able to do it, I don't read physical-changes-only into the spell at all, the fact that it brings the dead back to life implies that it does more than just revert the physical form. But either way my point was that mages can indeed &quot;temporarily&quot; erase any template that is gained later in life rather than being born/made with it, it's just a lot more fragile and prone to being dispelled than a lasting destruction of a template (like what archmasters can presumably do).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6365-fumus","name":"Fumus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6365_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-30T05:36:45-08:00","id":1040582,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hardwire99</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1039144-new-to-geist-lots-of-questions?p=1040570#post1040570\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So then Mages do have the ability to de-template someone with an Unmaking spell. So I would also put an ending spell from death in that same category if it targets the Bargain.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> No, short of archmastery-level magic mages cannot alter or remove major supernatural templates. Temporal Summoning can <i>temporarily</i> replace someone with a past version of themselves from before they were altered, and Rewrite History can <i>temporarily</i> alter the past so that they never got a template in the first place, but that's not the same as removing a major template.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Travis Stout<br /> Geist 2e Developer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12259-gimpinblack","name":"GimpInBlack","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"81"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-30T05:55:23-08:00","id":1040599,"title":"","content":"There is presidents to the contrary, Rewrite History is a 4 dot Patterning spell and it is not Archmastery, therefore it is conceivable that there are other ways of doing it without Archmastery. Please point out in the rules where it states that Only Archmaster level magic can do this including the statement that precludes Rewrite History. If you are going to make an absolute statement please back it up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-30T09:28:51-08:00","id":1040713,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hardwire99</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1039144-new-to-geist-lots-of-questions?p=1040599#post1040599\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There is presidents to the contrary, Rewrite History is a 4 dot Patterning spell and it is not Archmastery, therefore it is conceivable that there are other ways of doing it without Archmastery. Please point out in the rules where it states that Only Archmaster level magic can do this including the statement that precludes Rewrite History. If you are going to make an absolute statement please back it up.</div> </div> </div> </div>Read the spell.<br /> <br /> Making a supernatural being human again with Rewrite History requires that they not have been born to their condition, requires four Reach and a Mana to give the spell indefinite Duration and the ability to work on them at all, and is undoable with a one-dot spell.<br /> <br /> Archmastery is the level where <i>permanently removing a template</i> stands, and that type of spell requires components it takes whole stories to arrange for \u2014 the nearest equivalent is using Corridors of Time to make lasting changes to history that undo a transformation, which still has a hard lockout on any character who was a monster before you were born.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-30T11:40:33-08:00","id":1040791,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1039144-new-to-geist-lots-of-questions?p=1040713#post1040713\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Read the spell.<br /> <br /> Making a supernatural being human again with Rewrite History requires that they not have been born to their condition, requires four Reach and a Mana to give the spell indefinite Duration and the ability to work on them at all, and is undoable with a one-dot spell.<br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:blue\">Archmastery is the level where <i>permanently removing a template</i> stands, and that type of spell requires components it takes whole stories to arrange for</span></b>\u2014 the nearest equivalent is using Corridors of Time to make lasting changes to history that undo a transformation, which still has a hard lockout on any character who was a monster before you were born.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Highlighted part, of your statement, where is that in the book. I also do not see where it states that Rewrite History is the only spell capable of doing such.<br /> <br /> Here is a Fate spell that can undo an oath of a Supernatural creature, undoing a bargain isn't much of a stretch from there.<br /> <br /> Sever Oaths (Fate \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)<br /> Practice: Unraveling<br /> Primary Factor: Duration<br /> Withstand: Composure<br /> Suggested Rote Skills: Occult, Subterfuge, Weaponry<br /> To an Adept of Fate, all fetters on a being\u2019s free will are ultimately<br /> breakable, and oaths can be renegotiated. The mage<br /> may apply a number of the following effects equal to Potency:<br /> \u2022 Free a bound ephemeral entity, or soul.<br /> \u2022 Change the effects of an active boon or hex.<br /> \u2022 <b>Modify or negate an oath or other supernatural agreement<br /> reinforced by the dictates of Fate</b>.<br /> \u2022 Change or dispel a conditional trigger.<br /> \u2022 Modify the Doom of a subject with the Destiny Merit.<br /> <b>+2 Reach: The spell\u2019s effects are Lasting.</b><br /> <br /> Here is an example of Creative Thaumaturgy for Death, Why wouldn't this work? If the Geist has the ability to end the Bargain then then Deaths purview over endings can make it end prematurely. If the bargain cannot be ended by the Geist, <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">voluntarily or otherwise, </span>then I would agree with you. But if it has an ending then it can be ended.<br /> <br /> End Bargain (Death \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)<br /> Practice: Unmaking<br /> Primary Factor: Duration<br /> Withstand: Geist Resistance<br /> Suggested Rote Skills: Law, Occult, Subterfuge.<br /> The subject Geist is forces to break the bargain with its host. This will temporarily remove all of the abilities for the duration of the spell. After the spell duration ends the Geist can strike the bargain once again strike a bargain with the host.<br /> +2 Reach: The spell\u2019s effects are Lasting and the Geist must find a different host.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-30T13:14:21-08:00","id":1040838,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hardwire99</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1039144-new-to-geist-lots-of-questions?p=1040791#post1040791\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Highlighted part, of your statement, where is that in the book. I also do not see where it states that Rewrite History is the only spell capable of doing such.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can't recall from 2e Core, but Imperial Mysteries talks extensively on pages 35-37 what is required to alter templates. You need at least Archmastery in Death to alter a Sin-Eater or Geist, and if you are specifically wanting to break the Bargain, that may take Archmastery of Fate too. Specifically, you need Seven Dots and the Practice of Entities.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-30T13:47:22-08:00","id":1040871,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Second Chances</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1039144-new-to-geist-lots-of-questions?p=1040838#post1040838\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I can't recall from 2e Core, but Imperial Mysteries talks extensively on pages 35-37 what is required to alter templates. You need at least Archmastery in Death to alter a Sin-Eater or Geist, and if you are specifically wanting to break the Bargain, that may take Archmastery of Fate too. Specifically, you need Seven Dots and the Practice of Entities.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> In 2e the Imperial Mysteries are talked about in detail on pages 251 - 252, And no where in there does it discuss being an Archmastery-level to alter a Sin-Eater or Geist, nor does it mention that you need 7 dots in death and a practice in Entities to accomplish it either. As I stated there is precedence in the 2e book to the contrary. in particular the Time spell Rewrite History a 4 dot spell.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-30T14:16:34-08:00","id":1040890,"title":"","content":"And spells, at least sub-archmastery, can be dispelled or otherwise broken, even with an otherwise indefinite duration. That includes Rewrite History. Ergo, temporary.<br /> And that's before getting into the weird grey area of whether or not the previously-accepted fluff of truly, completely retroactively changing an entity being the sole domain of archmasters and other entities of similar power as it was in 1e still applies. But it also feels like we're skirting dangerously close to, ah... once heavily-trodden and hotly-debated territory, a bit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I've got a bit of a bad habit of extensively editing my posts after the fact. Please try and bear with me...<br /> In case you're comfortable being more friendly and casual about things, my name's Seren, or Es/Es for short. They/Them or Fae/Faer, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3946-sconce","name":"Sconce","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"127"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-30T14:24:08-08:00","id":1040894,"title":"","content":"This is probably a question that will be better answered in the Crossover Chronicle in the future. In the meantime, perhaps it'd be best to accept the word of the Geist developer Travis (with the forum handle of GimpInBlack). I'm willing to bet it is a question that has been discussed by the Onyx Path crew.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12074-robert-d","name":"Robert D","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"434"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-30T14:25:22-08:00","id":1040896,"title":"","content":"Every single Dev who's been asked about Major Templates and Mages says it requires archmastery, including Dave, who runs all of 2e, and Travis, who is developing Geist and has weighed in on this very thread. That's good enough for me. And I'm certain it says it somewhere in 2e.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-30T14:35:09-08:00","id":1040901,"title":"","content":"I didn't realize that I was arguing this with a Dev, Still I contest that Death should be able to do it at least temporarily with an ending spell. But at this point lets just agree to disagree.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-30T17:51:23-08:00","id":1040999,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hardwire99</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1039144-new-to-geist-lots-of-questions?p=1040901#post1040901\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I didn't realize that I was arguing this with a Dev, Still I contest that Death should be able to do it at least temporarily with an ending spell. But at this point lets just agree to disagree.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, temporarily doing it is something that everyone agrees on. It's the part where making it Lasting in any form that's being contested here.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-30T18:03:31-08:00","id":1041006,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Second Chances</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1039144-new-to-geist-lots-of-questions?p=1040896#post1040896\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Every single Dev who's been asked about Major Templates and Mages says it requires archmastery, including Dave, who runs all of 2e, and Travis, who is developing Geist and has weighed in on this very thread. That's good enough for me. And I'm certain it says it somewhere in 2e.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> And Travis would know, because Rewrite History was his idea when we were working on Mage 2e.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-30T20:56:21-08:00","id":1041092,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hardwire99</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1039144-new-to-geist-lots-of-questions?p=1040791#post1040791\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Here is a Fate spell that can undo an oath of a Supernatural creature, undoing a bargain isn't much of a stretch from there.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm aware of the content of Sever Oaths. It's also substantially more of a stretch to alter the framework of supernatural agreements that go don't <i>permanently change you into a supernatural creature or alter the nature of said supernatural creature.</i> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1017490-a-matter-of-iron?p=1022669#post1022669\">It's a more focused equivalent of Supernal Dispellation, not deep soul-surgery</a>.<br /> <br /> The Bargain doesn't impose any limitations on your actions or bind an ephemeral being any more stringently than an Anchor does, much less act as a &quot;fetter on free will.&quot; You can't <i>break</i> a Bargain, which is one of the big indicator's that it's not a little-b bargain.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hardwire99</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1039144-new-to-geist-lots-of-questions?p=1040901#post1040901\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I didn't realize that I was arguing this with a Dev</div> </div> </div> </div><i>It's the only thing in his signature besides his name.</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-31T00:42:49-08:00","id":1041140,"title":"","content":"The only time I read a signature is if it contains red in it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-31T01:46:05-08:00","id":1041151,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1039144-new-to-geist-lots-of-questions?p=1041006#post1041006\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> And Travis would know, because Rewrite History was his idea when we were working on Mage 2e.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I meant no disrespect to Travis, or to any one, I was using Rewrite History as an example of breaking a template temporarily. All I am trying to get to is if something like this would work. With Deaths purview over endings it should work, since the Bargain can be ended by the Geist at any time, this just forces that ending. I am willing to capitulate to the fact that only an Archmaster can do it permanently.<br /> <br /> End Bargain (Death \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)<br /> Practice: Unmaking<br /> Primary Factor: Duration<br /> Withstand: Geist Resistance<br /> Suggested Rote Skills: Law, Occult, Subterfuge.<br /> The subject Geist is forces to break the bargain with its host. This will temporarily remove all of the abilities for the duration of the spell. After the spell duration ends the Geist can once again strike a bargain with the host.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12259-gimpinblack\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12259\" data-vbnamecard=\"12259\">GimpInBlack</a> I apologize if I offended you, or anyone else here, I have never been one to take things on blind faith. That is all part and parcel of being an engineer.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-31T02:09:50-08:00","id":1041152,"title":"","content":"No offense taken. I wrote the creative thaumaturgy rules in Mage 2e, I should have remembered to include a &quot;What Magic Can't Do&quot; sidebar. :-)<br /> <br /> That spell would still not be possible. Short of Archmastery, Supernal magic cannot <i>directly</i> remove (or grant, for that matter) a major supernatural template, even temporarily.<br /> <br /> The reason Rewrite History works is because it's Time magic: it's not actually targeting the template, it's targeting the past itself. The name isn't just a fancy title, you are <i>literally</i> rewriting the subject's past so she never went to that goth nightclub and met that pale stranger with pointy teeth, or never got into that fatal car accident, or what have you. It doesn't cure vampirism, it retroactively makes it so the vampirism never happened at all. Time magic is weird that way.<br /> <br /> Your spell is directly targeting the Sin-Eater template and shutting it off. Magic can't do that. With Death, you could steal (or outright destroy) a Sin-Eater's Plasm pool, ward against their Haunts and innate abilities, and countermand some of their magic (e.g. if a Sin-Eater gives an area the Open Condition, Death magic could remove it again), but you can't just wholesale say &quot;your Bargain no longer exists,&quot; even temporarily.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Travis Stout<br /> Geist 2e Developer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12259-gimpinblack","name":"GimpInBlack","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"81"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-31T02:19:32-08:00","id":1041154,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GimpInBlack</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1039144-new-to-geist-lots-of-questions?p=1041152#post1041152\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No offense taken. I wrote the creative thaumaturgy rules in Mage 2e, I should have remembered to include a &quot;What Magic Can't Do&quot; sidebar. :-)<br /> <br /> That spell would still not be possible. Short of Archmastery, Supernal magic cannot <i>directly</i> remove (or grant, for that matter) a major supernatural template, even temporarily.<br /> <br /> The reason Rewrite History works is because it's Time magic: it's not actually targeting the template, it's targeting the past itself. The name isn't just a fancy title, you are <i>literally</i> rewriting the subject's past so she never went to that goth nightclub and met that pale stranger with pointy teeth, or never got into that fatal car accident, or what have you. It doesn't cure vampirism, it retroactively makes it so the vampirism never happened at all. Time magic is weird that way.<br /> <br /> Your spell is directly targeting the Sin-Eater template and shutting it off. Magic can't do that. With Death, you could steal (or outright destroy) a Sin-Eater's Plasm pool, ward against their Haunts and innate abilities, and countermand some of their magic (e.g. if a Sin-Eater gives an area the Open Condition, Death magic could remove it again), but you can't just wholesale say &quot;your Bargain no longer exists,&quot; even temporarily.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Got it and thanks for the clarification as to why Time is able to do it. Is Rewrite History lasting in that respect? If they never met that Vampire then when the magic ends the lingering results are still not meeting the Vampire.<br /> <br /> I like the additional aspects of death that you added.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-31T02:33:40-08:00","id":1041155,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hardwire99</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1039144-new-to-geist-lots-of-questions?p=1041154#post1041154\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Got it and thanks for the clarification as to why Time is able to do it. Is Rewrite History lasting in that respect? If they never met that Vampire then when the magic ends the lingering results are still not meeting the Vampire.<br /> <br /> I like the additional aspects of death that you added.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nope, Rewrite History isn't Lasting, and can't be made so. The best you can do is push it up to Indefinite, which means it will last forever unless something dispels it, but as it says in the spell's description, after the Duration expires the original history reasserts itself.<br /> <br /> The only way to make such a change Lasting is to actually travel back in time and make the change manually. However, given that the only time travel spell in the book, Shifting Sands, only lets you travel back a few turns (or scenes with Reach), that's only really practical for very recent events.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Travis Stout<br /> Geist 2e Developer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12259-gimpinblack","name":"GimpInBlack","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"81"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-31T03:28:28-08:00","id":1041171,"title":"","content":"Cool and thanks. If you ever come up with that list of what Magic Cannot Do I would be very interested.<br /> <br /> Now off magic and back to the topic of Geist, this is a Geist thread after all.<br /> <br /> Sin-Eaters will now have haunts, any spoilers would be great, will they also have Manifestations/Numina, will they have influence over lesser ghosts, We know, or at least believe, that they can eat ghosts can they also grant/remove Manifestations /Numina to other Ghosts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-31T03:45:20-08:00","id":1041176,"title":"","content":"Manifestations and Numina are specifically for ephemeral entities. Sin-Eaters aren't ephemeral entities, so no, they don't have those.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Travis Stout<br /> Geist 2e Developer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12259-gimpinblack","name":"GimpInBlack","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"81"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-31T04:32:10-08:00","id":1041192,"title":"","content":"Ok so when a Geist joins with a host he looses his Ehemeal status and all that is associated with that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-31T07:04:08-08:00","id":1041237,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hardwire99</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1039144-new-to-geist-lots-of-questions?p=1041192#post1041192\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok so when a Geist joins with a host he looses his Ehemeal status and all that is associated with that.</div> </div> </div> </div>If it is like first Edition, then yes. They trade those for being an unassailable immortal &quot;angel or devil on the shoulder&quot; if you will. Sin Eaters make very good fortresses to reside in. Also the view (of the mortal world) from within the fortress is much better than being sucked back down into the Underworld.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":3279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","user":"Pale_Crusader","date":". 01-31-2017, 10:06 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-31T07:26:33-08:00","id":1041244,"title":"","content":"Cool go to know. So look at the two conjoined as a single entity not ghost not human.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-31T07:43:01-08:00","id":1041248,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GimpInBlack</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1039144-new-to-geist-lots-of-questions?p=1041155#post1041155\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Nope, Rewrite History isn't Lasting, and can't be made so. The best you can do is push it up to Indefinite, which means it will last forever unless something dispels it, but as it says in the spell's description, after the Duration expires the original history reasserts itself.<br /> <br /> The only way to make such a change Lasting is to actually travel back in time and make the change manually. However, given that the only time travel spell in the book, Shifting Sands, only lets you travel back a few turns (or scenes with Reach), that's only really practical for very recent events.</div> </div> </div> </div>There <i>is </i>Corridors of Time, although that spell comes with its own set of difficulties and is limited to one's lifetime.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-02T01:00:37-08:00","id":1042270,"title":"","content":"Addendum to the original post: After some discussion and consideration, the answer to question 4 has been changed to &quot;No, but it doesn't seem to bother them much.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Travis Stout<br /> Geist 2e Developer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12259-gimpinblack","name":"GimpInBlack","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"81"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-02T01:40:14-08:00","id":1042281,"title":"","content":"They did die, after all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-02T01:53:17-08:00","id":1042285,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GimpInBlack</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1039144-new-to-geist-lots-of-questions?p=1042270#post1042270\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Addendum to the original post: After some discussion and consideration, the answer to question 4 has been changed to &quot;No, but it doesn't seem to bother them much.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1039144-new-to-geist-lots-of-questions?p=1042281#post1042281\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They did die, after all.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bOk so then a Death Mage looking at their soul would see none, So can they be a vessel for putting a soul into like treating the Sin-Eater as a Soul Jar? With the Geist in the Souless body they are already possessed (with special conditions like no removing the possession) so they can't be possessed. They are not dead. Are they then Immune to the Souless condition tree?<br /> <br /> So they are what the Tremere are trying to become.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12802,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","user":"Hardwire99","date":". 02-02-2017, 04:55 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-02T02:17:10-08:00","id":1042296,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hardwire99</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1039144-new-to-geist-lots-of-questions?p=1042285#post1042285\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> \u200bOk so then a Death Mage looking at their soul would see none, So can they be a vessel for putting a soul into like treating the Sin-Eater as a Soul Jar? With the Geist in the Souless body they are already possessed (with special conditions like no removing the possession) so they can't be possessed. They are not dead. Are they then Immune to the Souless condition tree?<br /> <br /> So they are what the Tremere are trying to become.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> They have something where a soul normally is, so no, you can't treat them as an empty vessel. The Soulless Conditions don't apply to them any more than they apply to, say, vampires or demons.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Travis Stout<br /> Geist 2e Developer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12259-gimpinblack","name":"GimpInBlack","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"81"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-02T02:23:07-08:00","id":1042299,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GimpInBlack</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1039144-new-to-geist-lots-of-questions?p=1042296#post1042296\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> They have something where a soul normally is, so no, you can't treat them as an empty vessel. The Soulless Conditions don't apply to them any more than they apply to, say, vampires or demons.</div> </div> </div> </div>Just as a point of clarification...the way you worded that, &quot;something where a soul normally is,&quot; makes it sound like Sin-Eaters don't actually have souls/their own souls anymore? Or do you just mean that their souls, while there, are altered because of the new connection with their geists?<br /> <br /> Edit